WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.670
The Species Comparison tool allows you to
compare human pathways with other species

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:15.660
to see what is common to both or perhaps missing
in humans or in the model organism.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.930
Species comparison is launched using the ‘Analyse
Data’ button in the Pathway browser header

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:24.390
bar or the Analyze button at the top of the
Pathway Browser.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:29.930
In the Species comparison section, select
one of the species in the dropdown list.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.009
Click the ‘Go’ button.

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:37.050
Reactome uses the manually curated human pathways
to computationally infer their equivalents

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.110
in other species.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:45.899
This inference process is based on gene orthology,
using the Ensembl Compara database.

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:51.210
Biological processes are remarkably well-conserved
over large evolutionary distances.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:56.230
Even though our focus is to annotate the molecular
details of human biological events, we can

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:00.870
use protein sequence orthology relationships
to ask whether the human proteins involved

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.589
in the reaction have orthologs in the model
organism.

00:01:04.589 --> 00:01:10.230
If the orthologs exist in the Ensembl Compara
resource, we computationally infer the corresponding

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:14.820
reaction for the model organism and in this
way build up a predicted pathway knowledgebase

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.980
for the organism.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:21.360
Clicking on pathway nodes displays the relevant
pathway diagram.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.400
The colour of reaction objects indicates the
result of the comparison:

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.820
o Yellow indicates that the protein has an
inferred equivalent in the comparison species

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:35.890
o Blue indicates that no equivalent was identified.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.770
This protein may not exist in the comparison
species

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:43.860
o No colour indicates that inference was not
possible.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:48.570
This is always the case for small molecules,
DNA and other objects that have no UniProt

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:53.310
entry
o Objects with bands of colour represent complexes

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:56.570
or sets containing more than one molecule.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:00.670
The bands of colour reflect the inference
success for the molecules within the complex

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:04.640
or set
o The species comparison bar at the bottom

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:10.119
of the Pathway diagram can be used to turn
off Species comparison colouring.

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:14.709
To see the Species comparison results for
the components of a complex, hover your mouse

00:02:14.709 --> 00:02:18.220
over the object and open the information panel.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:22.879
Traditionally, reactions in Reactome represent
events that occur within a single generic

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:24.560
human cell.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:30.250
It would, however, be useful to classify reactions
into different human tissue types, as to provide

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:36.269
an evolving picture of the reactions and pathways
in different cell- and tissue-specific environments.

00:02:36.269 --> 00:02:40.740
This tool allows users to understand the pathways
that are enriched in different human tissue

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.530
types based on protein expression data.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.599
Tissue Distribution is launched using the
Analysis button in the Pathway Browser header

00:02:48.599 --> 00:02:50.090
bar.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:56.809
In the Tissue Distribution section, select
the one experimental tissue dataset [HPA (E-PROT-3)

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:59.549
– Expression Atlas] in the drop-down list.

00:02:59.549 --> 00:03:03.989
We have imported protein expression in different
cell or tissue types from the Human Protein

00:03:03.989 --> 00:03:10.040
Atlas (HPA), overlaid these proteins on Reactome
data, and extracted the subset of reactions

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.650
for that particular cell type.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:18.099
The HPA data reflecting the expression of
the protein-coding genes in 44 different human

00:03:18.099 --> 00:03:21.620
tissues can be visualized through the Analysis
tools.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:26.489
Once the window refreshes, select the ‘Available
Tissues’ in the left panel and hit the ‘Add’

00:03:26.489 --> 00:03:30.409
button to add tissue expression data to the
analysis tool.

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:35.650
Press the “Add All’ button, if you would
like to adjoin all the tissue expression data.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:39.379
Use the ‘Remove all’ and ‘Remove’
buttons to delete tissue expression data from

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:41.400
the filter list.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.879
Once you have selected all the appropriate
tissues, click the Go button to start the

00:03:45.879 --> 00:03:47.219
analysis.

00:03:47.219 --> 00:03:52.290
An over-representation analysis is performed
on the protein expression data of each tissue

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.670
type.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:04:00.390
The results of the Tissue Distribution analysis
are presented similar to that of over-representation.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:04.669
Users can use the slider at the bottom of
the diagram panel to toggle between the selected

00:04:04.669 --> 00:04:06.549
tissue types.

00:04:06.549 --> 00:04:11.379
The Analysis tab in the details panel contains
the enrichment statistics and the diagram

00:04:11.379 --> 00:04:17.450
panel displays reactions or pathways with
overlaid tissue-specific expression data.

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:22.840
There are several options available to export
analysis results in various formats.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:28.310
The Downloads button is located at the left
of the Analysis tab in the Details panel.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.600
The following files can be downloaded.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:34.980
o Complete or filtered analysis results in
CSV format

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:42.620
o Complete analysis results in JSON format
o Identifier mappings of submitted data and

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:46.230
selected resource used for analysis in CSV
format

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:54.600
o A detailed report of the analysis for top
25 most significant pathways in PDF format

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:59.020
o A list of submitted identifiers that were
not found in CSV format

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:04.280
Analysis results overlaid on pathways and
reactions can also be downloaded using the

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:07.450
Export button in the Diagram panel.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:12.480
This feature takes a screenshot of the current
Diagram panel, which can be saved in PNG,

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:16.430
JPEG, SVG or PDF formats.

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:21.650
Analysis results on the voronoi pathways view
can also be downloaded using the Export button

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:22.479
in the page.

